[[
    BORDER 0 : PAPER 0 : INK 7 : BRIGHT 1 : FLASH 0 : CLEAR

    /* Register the native routine. A relative path is resolved relative to
       this .cyd file's folder. IMPORT is a compile-time declaration, like
       DECLARE or CONST. */
    IMPORT peek FROM "peek.asm"

    DECLARE 0 as addr_lo
    DECLARE 1 as addr_hi
    DECLARE 2 as result

    /* Ask the native routine for the byte at address 0000h (the first ROM
       byte). Arguments and the result travel through the variable array. */
    SET addr_lo TO 0
    SET addr_hi TO 0
    CALL peek
]]Native IMPORT / CALL demo (48K)
===============================

A native Z80 routine just read the byte stored at address 0000h and left it
in a CYD variable - something the virtual machine cannot do on its own.

[[
    IF @result = 243 THEN
        ]]Its value is 243 (0F3h), which is "DI", the first instruction of the
48K ROM. The native routine worked.[[
    ELSE
        ]]Its value is not 243. That is expected if you are not running this on
a plain 48K model.[[
    ENDIF
    NEWLINE : NEWLINE
    ]]Press any key to finish.[[
    WAITKEY
    CLEAR
    END
]]
